# -*- coding: utf-8 -*-
"""CRGO 0.9.0, second part: the GRCA sprint (decisions G1-G5, 2026-10-11) and the remaining-gaps packages R4-R8
(decisions R-a to R-d, 2026-10-11). Same tuple layouts as spec_v09.py.

New modules (decision G2; decision D2 still holds: the four 0.8.0 modules are unchanged)
  governance  governing bodies and committees, Three Lines roles, temporal role assignments, delegation, policy
              hierarchy and exceptions, decision records, oversight, independence          (imports grc)
  assurance   typed evidence and its metadata, sufficiency, external assurance reports, control effectiveness
              (design, implementation, operation), deficiencies, populations and sampling   (imports governance)
  audit       audit universe, plan, engagement, programme, procedure, evidence request, monitoring exception,
              finding, conclusion, report, recommendation, management response, corrective action, follow-up,
              closure and reopening                                                        (imports assurance)
  incident    security events, alerts, incident confirmation, reportable-breach assessment, timeline, lessons
              learned (package R8, minimal)                                                (imports evidence, org)
Additions to modules introduced earlier in 0.9.0 (not to the four 0.8.0 modules)
  evidence    knowledge status, source access status, evidence quality, estimate distributions, analytical
              hypotheses, analytical results from external models (DSS contract, ADR-007)
  grc         assessment methods, control assessor line, instrument versions, amendments, regulatory change,
              reassessment triggers, nonconformities, evidence requirements, obligated-party role
  mapping     narrower than, broader than, partially overlaps, supports compliance with, fulfils criterion,
              evaluates control

Licensed standards (IIA, ISACA, ISO, AICPA, COSO) are cited by identifier only; no text is reproduced (decision R-d).
Every term is proposed until the project owner approves it: the 0.9.0 group approvals of 2026-10-11 cover only the
terms that existed then (src/build.py, GROUP_SCOPE).
"""
